    description: "**Mechanism.** Of 46 library_export entrypoints, 45/46 targets carry supply_chain.is_exported=True; ONE has is_exported=False: label 'Library export: fold_string_interpolation._sub', symbol_id python:.../url_folding/__init__.py:113-117:fold_string_interpolation._sub:function, modifiers=['private'], conf 0.231. Source (__init__.py:113-117): _sub is a LOCAL closure defined inside fold_string_interpolation, used only as the callback to slot_re.sub(_sub, template) — unreachable from outside, cannot be imported. entrypoints.py:778-795 fires LIBRARY_EXPORT whenever a concept_type=='library_export' concept matches a symbol; the branch trusts the concept match and does NOT verify the symbol is module-level/exported (it cannot use Symbol.is_exported — None for 100% of nodes per WI-bujot). The 0.231 survives MIN_ENTRYPOINT_CONFIDENCE=0.10.\n\n**Evidence.** Fresh hypergumbo run on a /tmp fixture replicating fold_string_interpolation + nested _sub: the detector classifies the nested _sub as an entrypoint (connectivity_based, conf 0.5, 'High-connectivity python function: fold_string_interpolation._sub') — confirming the detector applies entrypoint-kind concepts to nested inner functions regardless of kind.\n\n**Consequence.** A consumer enumerating the public library API via kind=library_export EPs is handed a non-importable private nested helper; an agent seeding a reachability BFS from 'library exports' seeds a closure with no external callers.\n\n**Related (distinct).** Distinct from WI-lutad (confidence ranges), WI-dojor (in-degree boost), WI-popok (test-file heuristic), WI-pupiz (cli_command), WI-tuvun (main_function target overload) — none records library_export firing on a nested/private non-exported symbol. Source: dogfood_tranche_07 F128.A1, fresh-run reproduced."  # 887d
